{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ColoredJonesRecurrence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColoredJonesRecurrence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColoredJonesRecurrence.trace_recurrence_of_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColoredJonesRecurrence.trace_recurrence_of_relation","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColoredJonesRecurrence.lean#L51-L61","doc":"**Colored-Jones / closure recurrence.** Applying the (linear) Markov trace — the closure\nof the tangle, i.e. the knot invariant — to `pow_recurrence_of_relation` gives the\ninvariant's order-`d` recurrence: `tr(M^{n+d}) = ∑_{k<d} c_k · tr(M^{n+k})`. The recurrence\noperator is the quantum A-polynomial (AJ). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColoredJonesRecurrence.pow_recurrence_of_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColoredJonesRecurrence.pow_recurrence_of_relation","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColoredJonesRecurrence.lean#L39-L49","doc":"**Power recurrence from a monic relation.** If a knot operator `M` satisfies\n`M^d = ∑_{k<d} c_k · M^k` (its degree-`d` Cayley–Hamilton relation), then its powers obey the\norder-`d` linear recurrence `M^{n+d} = ∑_{k<d} c_k · M^{n+k}`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}